*.pyc
__pycache__/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# muni.db itself is never committed: once 2FA setup completes it also
# holds the live TOTP secret in auth_totp. The genuinely static,
# safe-to-ship part — municipalities, meetings, packets, blocked_sources —
# gets exported into the separately committed data/muni_seed.db via
# src/export_seed_db.py instead; a fresh deployment copies that in as its
# starting muni.db and grows its own live secrets from there.
data/muni.db
data/muni.db-wal
data/muni.db-shm

# Flask session-signing key — a live security secret, same reasoning as
# muni.db's auth_totp table above.
data/.flask_secret_key

# Runtime logs, not source.
data/*.log

# Real generated invoices (personal/business documents), not source.
data/invoice_backups/
